66 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 53 0 R
/E (As we delve into the realm of autonomous transportation, the focus shifts towards developing advanced mechanisms that transcend the limitations of traditional line-following vehicles. While these vehicles are adept at navigating predefined paths, their applications become constrained in dynamic environments. To overcome this, engineers are exploring a spectrum of sensor technologies, including lidar, ultrasonic, and cameras, to enhance the perception capabilities of autonomous vehicles. These sensors enable vehicles to dynamically adapt to their surroundings, paving the way for more versatile and adaptable autonomous transportation systems. The increasing demand for such systems aligns with the broader trend of creating safer, more efficient, and environmentally friendly modes of transportation. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
